        "name": "rampart-20x-playground application flow v0.2.0",
        "dimensions": {}
      },
      "batch_node": {
        "source": "tap_plugin.rampart_20x_playground.grift.application-flow",
        "name": "rampart-20x-playground application flow v0.2.0",
        "description": "MOCK DATA, never collected from a live system: what runs inside the two web tasks and the customer traffic that reaches them. One ECS container per web task (aws_core, real-shaped ARNs, the image reference and digest of the git-serious web image), the RUNS_TASK edges from the service and the cluster to each task, RUNS_CONTAINER from each task to its container, RUNS_IMAGE from each container to the one image host, RUNS_PROGRAM from each container to its gunicorn and from gunicorn to tap-web (the programs are in the inventory entities bundle), LOADS_LIBRARY from web task b's tap-web to the two libraries web task a's loads (openssl-fips-provider and cryptography, from the inventory software bundle), and ONE application flow (computing_core, keyless, so it carries its own fixed entity id) from the customer's computer to the gunicorn program of web task a (the program the container runs, which runs tap-web), stamped dataclass.customer=data. Only web task a's container and programs and the flow are marked overview=shown: web task b is the stacked copy of a. Every entity carries dcom=design. Import after the mock inventory, the inventory entities and the inventory software bundles. v0.2.0 adds four more application flows (all keyless, overview=shown): the database traffic from tap-web to the PostgreSQL program (dataclass.customer=data), the administration from the administrator's workstation to the authorization boundary's perimeter (dataclass.infra=admin), the developer's laptop to github.com and the terraform source puller to github.com (both dataclass.infra=code), their eight APPLICATION_FLOW_SOURCE and APPLICATION_FLOW_DESTINATION edges, and the RUNS_PROGRAM edge from the RDS instance to the PostgreSQL program (the database engine runs inside the managed instance). Overview nits 3: the flows are renamed 'customer data' and 'database'; the original administration flow (which ends on the authorization boundary and whose destination edge cannot change) is retired by dropping its overview=shown dimension, and a NEW administration flow (own fixed id) runs from the administrator's workstation to the teleport EC2 instance (dataclass.infra=admin); every shown flow carries icon_angle (degrees, 0 north, 90 east, 180 south, 270 west) for the direction its icon and arrowhead point. Dimension pack v0.6.0 stamps: each of the five stamped application flows carries dataclass.action=transmit, the database flow carries dataclass.customer=sanitized (the customer data flow keeps data), and the two ECS containers carry dataclass.action=process; the retired administration flow stays unstamped."
      },
